{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "09", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "08", "M": "28", "S": "08"}}, "news": [{"title": "Registration opens for 460 plots in Lucknow development body's Anant Nagar", "para": "Online registration for 460 plots in Lucknow's Anant Nagar scheme is now open.  These plots, ranging from 112.5 to 200 square metres, will be allotted through a lottery.  The Anant Nagar scheme is being developed along Mohan Road with wide roads and green spaces.  LDA will also conduct a lottery for 407 housing units on August 14.  Previously, the authority allotted 75 flats in Park View and Aishbagh Square apartments.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/registration-opens-for-460-plots-in-lucknow-development-bodys-anant-nagar/133063254?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-263930/133063254.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "Andhra Pradesh rolls out fresh incentives for IGBC-certified green projects", "para": "Andhra Pradesh has rolled out new concessions on development fees specifically tailored for green buildings. Developers of silver-rated projects will receive a five percent discount, while those achieving a gold rating can look forward to a ten percent reduction. Platinum-rated projects are rewarded handsomely with a fifteen percent concession.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/andhra-pradesh-rolls-out-fresh-incentives-for-igbc-certified-green-projects/133063128?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-111714/133063128.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Birla Estates' subsidiary buys FSI from Parinee entities for \u20b9159 crore", "para": "Birla Estates has successfully acquired almost 90,000 sq ft of FSI for over Rs 159 crore, a strategic move aimed at bolstering their society redevelopment efforts in Khar, Mumbai. This FSI was secured via a Slum Rehabilitation Authority scheme from Kandivali. The development rights will be transferred and applied to a larger property in Khar, enhancing the region's premium living environment.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/birla-estates-subsidiary-buys-fsi-from-parinee-entities-for-159-crore/133063094?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-417734/133063094.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}]}